From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Grasso <code@danielgrasso.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:31:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(color): decode untagged SDR with sdr_transfer while
 an SDR gamut mapping is staged

Untagged SDR content was decoded with the piecewise sRGB curve whenever
the output was not PQ, so a staged sdr_gamut = "srgb" mapping into a
gamma 2.2 panel lifted its shadows (64 came out as 66, #121212 as
#191919). The sdr_transfer setting already chooses the decode curve for
HDR outputs; it now applies while an SDR gamut mapping is staged too.
A gamma ramp alone keeps the encoded sRGB path.
---
 docs/user/display-features.md          |  2 +-
 umbrielfx/render/fx_renderer/fx_pass.c | 10 +++++++---
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/user/display-features.md b/docs/user/display-features.md
index 085eddc6..fba668eb 100644
--- a/docs/user/display-features.md
+++ b/docs/user/display-features.md
@@ -128,7 +128,7 @@ hdr = "on"
 sdr_transfer = "srgb"
 ```
 
-The choice applies on reload and only while that output uses HDR (PQ). It also keeps effect color controls and SDR capture encoding consistent with the chosen curve. Explicit client color descriptions keep their declared transfer function, including piecewise sRGB, gamma 2.2, PQ, and linear content. The display's PQ encoding and normal SDR rendering stay unchanged. Run `umbriel color` to inspect each output's configured `sdr_transfer` choice, which stays inert while the output renders SDR.
+The choice applies on reload, while that output uses HDR (PQ) and while an SDR gamut mapping is staged (`sdr_gamut = "srgb"` with a characterized panel): untagged SDR is then decoded with this curve before it is mapped into the panel, so a gamma 2.2 panel keeps its shadows. Without either, untagged SDR passes through encoded. It also keeps effect color controls and SDR capture encoding consistent with the chosen curve. Explicit client color descriptions keep their declared transfer function, including piecewise sRGB, gamma 2.2, PQ, and linear content. The display's PQ encoding and normal SDR rendering stay unchanged. Run `umbriel color` to inspect each output's configured `sdr_transfer` choice, which stays inert while the output renders SDR.
 
 `sdr_white` can also be selected for one running output without editing the configuration:
 
diff --git a/umbrielfx/render/fx_renderer/fx_pass.c b/umbrielfx/render/fx_renderer/fx_pass.c
index 5fac188e..0bd617f2 100644
--- a/umbrielfx/render/fx_renderer/fx_pass.c
+++ b/umbrielfx/render/fx_renderer/fx_pass.c
@@ -3400,9 +3400,13 @@ struct fx_gles_render_pass* fx_begin_buffer_pass(
       return NULL;
     }
     // The supplied transform's EOTF stage says how the frame is written, not
-    // how its content is decoded: untagged SDR is sRGB, so only a PQ
-    // destination reselects the SDR decode curve (the sdr_transfer setting).
-    if (state.tf == WLR_COLOR_TRANSFER_FUNCTION_ST2084_PQ) {
+    // how its content is decoded. A PQ destination, or a staged SDR gamut
+    // mapping (a matrix into the panel's colorimetry), reselects the SDR
+    // decode curve (the sdr_transfer setting): untagged SDR was made for a
+    // display that applies its own curve, gamma 2.2 by default, and decoding
+    // it as piecewise sRGB would lift the shadows of a gamma 2.2 panel. A
+    // gamma ramp alone keeps sRGB, the encoded path it was built on.
+    if (state.tf == WLR_COLOR_TRANSFER_FUNCTION_ST2084_PQ || state.has_matrix) {
       sdr_tf = pq_sdr_transfer;
     }
     struct wlr_allocator* allocator = output_buffers != NULL ? output_buffers->allocator : renderer->allocator;
